<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices ease on rising arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices ease on rising arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices fell on rising arrivals on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said soyoil solvent was up by 300 rupees per tonne on better demand while soyoil refined was steady. Business volume was dull and undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $280 per tonne in ready delivery and was $275-276 per tonne for normal December and January shipment in new season.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $125 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,200 rupees FOR Bedibunder and 4,150-4,175 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
